+# 194 · A bulk order's quote event sent twice, refuted on the route's trace in exact order
+
+[← All examples](../README.md)
+
+| Verdict | Categories | Severity if shipped | Change | Verified unit | Approach |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **✗ Violation: counterexample found** | functional | high | refactor, behaviour change not intended | [`QuotesController#quote`](../../examples/apps/shop/src/main/java/shop/QuotesController.java) | [B9: Regression verification](../../lib/README.md) |
+
+> The value-object refactor of 190, with the route sending the `QuoteEvent` a second time for an order of ten items or more. The answer is the same, and so is the last event sent, which is what a test of a producer usually checks. The tool compares the whole ordered trace of sends and refutes it on a ten-item order, the witness replayed on the JVM under recording stubs.
+
+Tags: [payments](../README.md#tag-payments), [spring-boot](../README.md#tag-spring-boot), [messaging](../README.md#tag-messaging), [duplicate-delivery](../README.md#tag-duplicate-delivery), [joint-run](../README.md#tag-joint-run), [effect-trace](../README.md#tag-effect-trace), [own-checker](../README.md#tag-own-checker)
+
+## The change
+
+`Quote`'s amount, a `long` of cents, becomes a value object, `Money`, so `Quote(long cents, int quantity)` is now `Quote(Money amount, int quantity)`; `Pricing.total` reads `q.amount.cents()` where it read `q.cents`; the pure helper `Pricing.discount` (a tenth off ten items or more) is rewritten as an early return; and the route `POST /quotes` makes the quote with `new Money(cents)`. Nothing is meant to change: not the total, not the event the route sends, not what `Pricing.withQuantity` hands back. In this version the route also sends the event again when `quantity >= 10`.
+
+**Before** ([`QuotesController.java`](../../examples/apps/shop/src/main/java/shop/QuotesController.java), line 16):
+
+```java
+
+    @PostMapping("/quotes")
+    public long quote(@RequestParam long cents, @RequestParam int quantity) {
+        long total = Pricing.total(new Quote(cents, quantity));
+        if (total > 0) kafka.send("quotes", new QuoteEvent(total, quantity));
+        return total;
+    }
+
+    /** The case this loop leaves unresolved: a string response, built by string concatenation. */
+    @PostMapping("/quotes/text")
+    public String quoteText(@RequestParam long cents, @RequestParam int quantity) {
+        return "total " + Pricing.total(new Quote(cents, quantity));
+    }
+}
+```
+
+**After:**
+
+```java
+
+    @PostMapping("/quotes")
+    public long quote(@RequestParam long cents, @RequestParam int quantity) {
+        long total = Pricing.total(new Quote(new Money(cents), quantity));
+        if (total > 0) {
+            kafka.send("quotes", new QuoteEvent(total, quantity));
+            if (quantity >= 10) kafka.send("quotes", new QuoteEvent(total, quantity));
+        }
+        return total;
+    }
+
+    /** The case this loop leaves unresolved: a string response, built by string concatenation. */
+    @PostMapping("/quotes/text")
+    public String quoteText(@RequestParam long cents, @RequestParam int quantity) {
+        return "total " + Pricing.total(new Quote(new Money(cents), quantity));
+    }
+}
+```
