+## Would the existing tests have caught it?
+
+No: every existing unit test passes (`java -ea shop.Tests`, run against the patched code).
+
+## Why it matters
+
+A duplicated send is invisible to the response and to a test that looks at the last record sent; downstream, the order is quoted twice.
+
+## Why the verdict is right
+
+The trace of modeled calls is compared in exact order, every attempt with its payload as it was at the call, so two equal events are two attempts, not one. On a quote of ten or more items with a positive total, the old build attempts one send and the new one two.
+
+## What to do
+
+Send the event once.
